{"id":"tictoc-unnecessary-abort-detection","benchmark":"skillsbench","instruction":"The famous TicToc concurrency-control mechanism can sometimes abort transactions that did not actually need to abort and could have been left in execution. Your task is to identify the policy of detecting every unnecessary abort.\n\nYou are given a trace from a TicToc workload to test if you can detect unnecessary aborts. It's from YCSB KV transaction workload. The trace data is available in `/root/traces/` and contains two tab-separated TSV files with no header. All fields are unsigned decimal integers.\n\n`writes.tsv` contains the writes made by the transactions.\n\n`writes.tsv` columns:\n\n1. `txn_seq` - transaction id.\n2. `key_hash` - 64-bit key.\n3. `new_wts` - write timestamp installed by the committing transaction; same as `commit_ts` for that write.\n4. `ats_at_write` - per-key access counter value observed when this write is recorded.\n\n`aborts.tsv` contains the aborts made by the transactions.\n\n`aborts.tsv` columns:\n\n1. `txn_seq` - transaction id.\n2. `key_hash` - 64-bit key.\n3. `local_wts` - WTS observed by the transaction when it read the key.\n4. `current_wts` - current global WTS of the key at validation time.\n5. `commit_ts` - candidate commit timestamp chosen for the validating transaction.\n6. `ats_at_abort` - per-key access counter value observed when the abort was logged.\n\n\nNote that the per-key access counter means the how many times a key is accessed (read, write) on the fly when reading it. `ats_at_abort` and `ats_at_write` use the same counter for a key, it just has different name and meaning in the two files.\nFurther, the read timestamp changes are not explicitly recorded in the trace, because they are not needed for the task.\n\nWrite a JSON file to `/root/unnecessary_aborts.json` containing a sorted ascending array of all transaction ids that were unnecessarily aborted. Each transaction id should appear at most once.\n\nThe output file must be a JSON array of unsigned integer transaction ids, formatted like:\n\n```json\n[\n  1000000000001,\n  1000000000002,\n  1000000000003,\n  1000000000004,\n  1000000000005,\n  1000000000006\n]\n\n```","supplemental":[],"items":[{"item_id":"IA-01","requirement":"Create the output file at the exact required path /root/unnecessary_aborts.json.","source_quote":"Write a JSON file to `/root/unnecessary_aborts.json`","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestTicTocUnnecessaryAbortDetection::test_output_file_exists","verification":"A grader can verify this by checking that a file exists on disk at /root/unnecessary_aborts.json after the agent finishes.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"IA-01","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"IA-02","requirement":"The file's top-level content must be a JSON array whose every element is an unsigned integer transaction id (no strings, floats, nulls, or nested objects).","source_quote":"The output file must be a JSON array of unsigned integer transaction ids","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestTicTocUnnecessaryAbortDetection::test_output_is_json_integer_array","verification":"A grader can verify this by loading /root/unnecessary_aborts.json as JSON and confirming the top-level value is a list whose every element is an integer.","notes":"The assertion only checks isinstance(int); it does not separately assert non-negativity, but correctly derived txn ids should naturally be unsigned per the input schema.","validation":{"item_id":"IA-02","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"IA-03","requirement":"The array must be sorted in strictly ascending order and each transaction id must appear at most once, even if that id has multiple rows in aborts.tsv.","source_quote":"a sorted ascending array of all transaction ids that were unnecessarily aborted. Each transaction id should appear at most once.","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestTicTocUnnecessaryAbortDetection::test_output_is_sorted_and_unique","verification":"A grader can verify this by loading the JSON array and checking that it equals its own ascending-sorted version and that its length equals the length of the set of its elements (no duplicates).","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"IA-03","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"IA-04","requirement":"Every transaction id in the output must correspond to a transaction that actually has at least one row in aborts.tsv, since only aborted transactions can have been unnecessarily aborted.","source_quote":"`aborts.tsv` contains the aborts made by the transactions.","verification_type":"generated","verification_ref":"check_ids_subset_of_aborted_txns","verification":"A grader can verify this by loading aborts.tsv and confirming every txn_seq value present in the output JSON array also appears as a txn_seq value in at least one row of aborts.tsv.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"IA-04","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"IA-05","requirement":"The output set of transaction ids must exactly match the true set of transactions whose abort was unnecessary under correct TicToc validation semantics, derived from the write and access-counter fields in writes.tsv and aborts.tsv (local_wts, current_wts, commit_ts, ats_at_abort, new_wts, ats_at_write), with no unnecessary aborts missing and no necessary aborts wrongly included.","source_quote":"identify the policy of detecting every unnecessary abort","verification_type":"generated","verification_ref":"check_unnecessary_abort_set_matches_reference","verification":"A grader can verify this by independently computing, from writes.tsv and aborts.tsv, the reference set of transaction ids whose abort was unnecessary under TicToc validation semantics, then checking that the submitted array is exactly equal (same elements, no more, no fewer) to that reference set.","notes":"The exact unnecessary-abort policy is not spelled out verbatim in the instructions and must be derived from field semantics (including that ats_at_write and ats_at_abort share the same per-key counter); the reference scoring script (score_outputs.py) implementing this comparison was not included in the provided verifier source, so this item cannot be anchored as an assertion.","validation":{"item_id":"IA-05","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}}],"runs":[{"id":"claude-code-no-skills__anthropic-claude-opus-4-7-src-2ef00c4||tictoc-unnecessary-abort-detection","label":"claude-code-no-skills · anthropic-claude-opus-4-7-src-2ef00c4","condition":"without skill","official":1.0,"raw":{"yes":4,"no":0,"abstain":1,"score":1.0,"coverage":0.8},"raw_answers":[{"item_id":"IA-01","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"IA-02","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"IA-03","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"IA-04","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"IA-05","answer":"ABSTAIN"}],"anchored":{"yes":5,"no":0,"abstain":1,"score":1.0,"coverage":0.8333333333333334},"anchored_answers":[{"item_id":"IA-01","answer":"YES","basis":"official-pass-rule"},{"item_id":"IA-02","answer":"YES","basis":"official-pass-rule"},{"item_id":"IA-03","answer":"YES","basis":"official-pass-rule"},{"item_id":"IA-04","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"IA-05","answer":"ABSTAIN","basis":"log-judgment"}],"raw_note":"Log-only judgments are from a separate archived rejudgment of the same run. The outcome-inclusive result is the original judging pass.","raw_source":"main_table/raw_backfill/results.jsonl:27","source":"main_table/leaderboard_all/results.jsonl:199","truncated":false},{"id":"claude-code-with-skills__anthropic-claude-opus-4-6-src-paper-v1||tictoc-unnecessary-abort-detection","label":"claude-code-with-skills · anthropic-claude-opus-4-6-src-paper-v1","condition":"with skill","official":1.0,"raw":{"yes":4,"no":0,"abstain":1,"score":1.0,"coverage":0.8},"raw_answers":[{"item_id":"IA-01","answer":"YES"